 Why not introduce weapons that are specific to a characters class. eg.
having an archeologist find a revolver with six shots, no other class
being able to work out how it works. Likewise have holy symbols that only
work for a correctly alligned priest, some kind of berserking weapon to
give bonuses to barbarians. 

 Also how about a book of gems to let other character classes id rocks (
provided they are smart enough to be able to read). Also have books to
likewise identify weapons & armour. Chemistry sets to identify potions.
 
 It would be nice if you could pay shopkeepers to identify items - have it
so they can only id. types that they sell. Why don't current shopkeepers
tell you what you are buying? I've heard of buyer beware but this is
excessive. 
 
  Why not be able to set your own traps- ie. find an unset bear trap
(possibly need strength to set it), find some explosives and set a
door trap ( in this case intelligence), even use a pickaxe or wand of
digging to build a pit.

 What ways can you get amnesia and forget things in Nethack ? It would be
great to hit the shopkeeper with some kind of amnesia potion so that they
will forget that you haven't paid for your purchases.

 Finally a wizard should be permitted to become a lich.

